{"title":"2013 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Mr. Matheson has four cards, numbered 1, 2, 3, 4. He gives one card each to Ben, Wendy, Riley, and Sara. Ben is not given the number 1. Wendy’s number is 1 greater than Riley’s number. Which number could Sara <i>not</i> have been given?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since Ben did not get a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, he must have gotten a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, or a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Wendy's number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> more than Riley's number, so Riley couldn't have been given a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>If Ben is given a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, this means that Riley must be given a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and Wendy must be given a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> because if Riley is given a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, then Ben's number would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> more than Riley's number, when it should be Wendy instead. This means that Sara would be given a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>If Ben is given a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, this means that Riley must be given a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and Wendy must be given a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> because if Riley is given a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, then Ben's number would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> more than Riley's number, when it should be Wendy instead. This means that Sara would be given a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>If Ben is given a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, this means that Riley must be given less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> because if Riley is given a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, then Ben's number would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> more than Riley's number, when it should be Wendy instead. This means that Riley has a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and Wendy has a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or Riley has a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and Wendy has a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. This means that Sara would be given a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Combining these, we can see that the only number that Sara couldn't have been given was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/e/b5e8656291085c388b48a0fa8da85aed21c483bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"20\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CSMC\" title=\"2013 CSMC\">2013 CSMC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CSMC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CSMC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CSMC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CSMC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_1\" title=\"2013 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 1\">Part A Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_3\" title=\"2013 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 3\">Part A Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_1\" title=\"2013 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 1\">Part A 1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Part A 2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_3\" title=\"2013 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 3\">Part A 3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 4 (page does not exist)\">Part A 4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">Part A 5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">Part A 6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 1 (page does not exist)\">Part B 1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 2 (page does not exist)\">Part B 2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">Part B 3</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=CEMC_Senior_Competition\" title=\"CEMC Senior Competition\">CEMC Senior Competition</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018055746\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.021 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.038 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 147/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1283/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 134/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4967/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.231      1 Template:CEMC_CIMC/CSMC_box\n100.00%    7.231      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:37299:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018055746 and revision id 287958. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}